  "headingOutline": [
    "H1: Redefining AI strategy for business.",
    "H2: AI strategy that’s practical, not prescriptive.",
    "H2: Bespoke AI strategy, aligned to your objectives.",
    "H2: Building blocks for lasting AI impact.",
    "H2: A clear AI roadmap, grounded in business needs.",
    "H2: AI strategies that are relied on by the world's best-run companies.",
    "H3: Delivering a practical AI & Automation roadmap to the UK Government’s Insolvency Service.",
    "H2: Meet the Aiimi experts.",
    "H2: A practical path to AI value.",
    "H2: Find out more about our Workplace AI platform and services.",
    "H2: Book your free 60-minute AI strategy call."
  ],
  "bodyText": "Redefining AI strategy for business.\n\nAI moves too fast for traditional strategies; it demands a fast-track, fluid approach that accelerates value delivery.\n\nTalk to us\nAI strategy that’s practical, not prescriptive.\n\nAI can transform your business, but without the right strategy, you'll only ever scratch the surface of what's possible. Built on years of deep industry expertise and cutting-edge technology, our approach to AI strategy is fast, adaptive, and practical. No laborious data engineering exercises. No rigid five-year plan.\n\n01/02\n\n\"Aiimi has given us the strongest possible footing to start our AI journey.\"\n\nNathan Marsh, Digital Innovation Lead\n\n\"AI capabilities are evolving at an unprecendented pace, leaving traditional strategies and maturity models outdated as soon they're published. We need to think about AI strategy in a different way to all previous strategies.\"\n\nSteve Salvin, CEO, Aiimi\n\nBespoke AI strategy, aligned to your objectives.\n\nFor some organisations, the focus of AI strategy might be on ethics, especially for those in the public sector or dealing with sensitive data. For others, it might be more about scaling internal AI capability or getting a grip on fragmented AI initiatives that are already underway.\n\nOur AI consultants work with each customer to shape a strategy and roadmap that fits their unique context, priorities, and readiness, to cover three core areas.\n\nAI Vision\n\nWe start by working with senior stakeholders to define a clear vision for AI. What role should it play? How does it connect to goals, market pressures, and competitor activity? Which teams and leaders does this matters to most, and what part will they play?\n\nPrinciples\n\nWe then agree on a set of principles for AI adoption - things like responsibility, transparency, and governance. These act as a shared compass, helping teams make consistent decisions about how AI should be used in practice as the organisation evolves.\n\nGame plan\n\nFinally, we shape a practical plan of attack for embedding AI. What’s in scope? What’s not? Where do we start, and who needs to be involved? This enables us to create a focused view of what happens next, tailored to where the organisation is right now and where it needs to get to.\n\nBuilding blocks for lasting AI impact.\n\nFrom AI literacy to iterative development – enablement and agility are key to our methodology. We know the best places to start, how to release value quickly, and how to set your people up for sustainable success.\n\nBook a free 60-minute AI strategy call\nA clear AI roadmap, grounded in business needs.\n\nOur strategic framework uncovers the areas where AI can help your people get to the answers they need faster, smarter. Then, assessing use cases by four key dimensions, we can build an AI roadmap with clarity, ready to experiment and scale.\n\nValue.\n\nAI should unlock better decisions, productivity gains, cost reduction, safety improvements, or something new. We plan how to measure impact and benchmark the current state, so you can see the difference AI makes.\n\nData.\n\nAI needs good data to succeed. We work out whether the right data exists to make this use case fly - and what kind of data governance work might be needed.\n\nRisk.\n\nAll AI comes with considerations - regulatory, compliance, or ethical. Risk could mean physical safety, IP exposure, or brand damage. We consider what guardrails you'd need to progress an AI use case.\n\nFeasibility & Cost.\n\nWhat would it actually take to go from AI prototype to AI that thousands of users can adopt safely and securely? We stay grounded in AI that's going to make an impact.\n\nAI strategies that are relied on by\nthe world's best-run companies.\nView all Case Studies\nDelivering a practical AI & Automation roadmap to the UK Government’s Insolvency Service.\nView Case Study\nMeet the\nAiimi experts.\n\nWe’re responsive and able to source the right team rapidly, so you get the A team every time – whether you’re facing an unprecedented event or need to jump on an opportunity. \n\nGet in touch with our Services team.\nA practical path to AI value.\n\nTurn AI ambitions into measurable impact, with our expert guide. Real-world examples show how AI can improve time to value, reduce costs, and deliverable measurable results. Learn how to assess use cases, define success metrics, and take the next steps with confidence.\n\nClick to download\nFind out more about our Workplace AI platform and services.\nResponsible AI.\nBuild & Scale AI.\nWorkplace AI Platform.\nAI Chat & Assistant.\nAI Data Governance.\nBook your free 60-minute AI strategy call.\n\nGet in touch for a free session with one of our AI strategy experts, tailored to your top priorities. To arrange a call or ask us anything, simply fill in the form and we'll be in touch within one working day.\n\nFirst Name*\nLast Name*\nEmail*\nPhone\nMessage\nHow did you first hear about us?\nPlease select\nSearch engine (e.g. Google, Bing)\nSocial media\nAI (ChatGPT, Copilot, Claude, etc)\nEvent or Webinar\nOnline advertisement\nNews or media article\nPodcast\nOfficial Aiimi Partner\nReview site (e.g. Gartner, G2)\nReferred by an Aiimi customer\nWord of mouth\nColleague or employer\nOther\nFrom time to time, we would like to contact you about our products, services, events and other content that we think will be of interest to you. You can unsubscribe from these communications at any time.\nYes please - I’d like to hear more from Aiimi!\nBy submitting this form you consent to us processing and storing the information you provide in accordance with our Privacy Policy\nSUBMIT"
}